### Page 1 of 1

```text
Amendments made and approved at the May 4th Finance Committee Meeting
RESOLUTION – Recommending a salary reduction for the City’s Governing Body.
(SPONSORS – MR. CASE, MR. COOK, MR. LUNA, DR. RINNE, MR. ROYBAL, MR.
SHANOR & MR. WHITE)

Amendment # 1

Amended by substitute authored by Councilman Shanor which revised the Now
Therefore, Be It Resolved clause by striking #1 and replacing it with:

The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne believes it is important for all members
of the Governing Body to lead by example and incur a reduction in pay commensurate
with the city department global percentage cut of 13% proposed in Mayor Orr’s FY
2021 budget proposal.

And by adding a new Section #2 in the Now, Therefore, Be It Resolved clause to read
as follows:

All members of the Governing Body are encouraged to remit 13% of their salaries to
the general fund each month of FY 2021 fiscal year.

Amendment #2

Amended by replacing “Governing Body” with “City Council”, removing the
Mayor….
Amendment #3

Amended the Now Therefore, Be It Resolved clause, Section 2, to read as follows: “All
members of the City Council are encouraged to remit 13% of their salaries which will
sunset on December 31, 2020”

Amendment #4

Amended the Now Therefore, Be It Resolved clause, Section 2, by replacing “general
fund” with “Forward Greater Cheyenne Emergency Relief Fund”
```
